coder › Done. Here's what I changed and the result.

## Changes

- **`src/redact.ts`** (new) — exports `redact<T>(value: T): T`.
  - Deep-copies arrays and plain objects (`Object.create(null)` included); primitives are returned as-is.
  - For each object key, it lowercases the name and redacts the whole value to `'[redacted]'` if it contains any of `password`, `passwd`, `secret`, `token`, `apikey`, `api_key`, `api-key`, or `authorization`.
  - Any string value elsewhere has `Bearer <token>` redacted to `Bearer [redacted]` (every occurrence, via `/Bearer \S+/g`).
  - Input is never mutated; non-sensitive values are unchanged.

- **`src/logger.ts`** — `log()` now builds the line from `{ level, message, ...redact(fields) }`, so fields are redacted before serialization. `message` itself is not passed through `redact`, per the request.

- **`src/redact.test.ts`** (new) — 7 tests: deep nesting, case-insensitive key matching, Bearer token redaction (including multiple tokens per string), unchanged non-sensitive values, input non-mutation, and copy semantics for objects/arrays.

- **`src/logger.test.ts`** — added a test asserting secrets in fields are redacted in the emitted JSON line.

## Check output

