Committed on `work/main` as `d98e620` ("Redact secrets in log fields"); working tree is clean.

## Decisions worth flagging

- I applied "in any case" only to the key-name matching, as written; the `Bearer ` match is literal and case-sensitive.
- I defined a Bearer token as the run of non-whitespace characters after `Bearer `, so `"got Bearer abc123 ok"` becomes `"got Bearer [redacted] ok"`. A token immediately followed by punctuation (e.g. `Bearer abc.`) would have the punctuation consumed as part of the token — say the word if you'd like that boundary tightened.
- Only the `fields` argument is redacted; `level` and `message` pass through untouched.

